// Push for the iPhone app: the value of the `aps-environment` entitlement.
//
// Resources/JunoMobile.entitlements reads it as $(JUNO_APS_ENVIRONMENT), and
// JunoMobile-Debug, -Stable and -Next include this file. Without the
// entitlement, `registerForRemoteNotifications` fails on every build, which
// silently kills agent, Work, research and Code approval pushes and
// "Continue on iPhone" (commit 615d3a5b0 dropped it once already).
// `npm run native:entitlements:check` fails CI when it goes missing again.
//
// The value follows the signing identity, because that is what decides the
// provisioning profile, and code signing refuses an entitlement the profile
// does not carry:
//
//   Apple Development   -> a development profile -> development
//   Apple Distribution  -> an App Store profile  -> production
//
// Today every configuration signs with Apple Development (Base.xcconfig), so
// Debug, Stable and Next all build with `development`. The App Store export in
// native/Scripts/release-ios.sh and release-ios.yml re-signs the archive with
// the distribution profile, which rewrites the value to `production` in the
// shipped app. A build signed directly with Apple Distribution gets
// `production` here without anyone editing a file. Anything unrecognised falls
// back to `development`, the value every development profile carries.
JUNO_APS_ENVIRONMENT_FOR_Apple_Development = development
JUNO_APS_ENVIRONMENT_FOR_iPhone_Developer = development
JUNO_APS_ENVIRONMENT_FOR_Apple_Distribution = production
JUNO_APS_ENVIRONMENT_FOR_iPhone_Distribution = production
JUNO_APS_ENVIRONMENT = $(JUNO_APS_ENVIRONMENT_FOR_$(CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY:c99extidentifier):default=development)
